; RoundEndHeap -- GL only (null card, the texture heap capped at 16 MB as on
; Hamiller's Radeon): many map changes in one run (ZOD_ROUNDEND 12: a round
; ends 12 s after its map was loaded, the next map 10 s later; orig01 and
; orig02 in turn, the next map unpaused). Does the texture heap grow with
; every map change? The library's "texture heap used ... allocations
; refused" and the game's "no room" lines decide. Music off (-u).
; LIMIT 600
FailAt 1000
Wait 5
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/zod-#?
Echo "0" >DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Echo "Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map" >>DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Echo "Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig02.map" >>DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
SetEnv ZOD_ROUNDEND 12
SetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax 16
Echo "=== GL (null card, 16 MB heap), many map changes ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZod rh1 200 -u -l DEV:Test/maps_round.txt
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-rh1.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-rh1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/zod-rh1-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
UnSetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax
UnSetEnv ZOD_ROUNDEND
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
